WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.200 --> 00:00:10.560
Ordinary life is getting a lot more expensive.&nbsp;
In an Fox News poll, 70 percent of registered&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:15.520
voters said recent increases in grocery prices&nbsp;
had caused hardship for them and their families,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:20.640
and 68 percent gave that response about gas&nbsp;
prices. Almost three in ten described the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:25.760
hardships as serious. In the poll, 86 percent&nbsp;
of registered voters said they were extremely or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:31.600
very concerned about inflation and higher prices.&nbsp;
Concern about it topped the list of the 13 items&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:36.640
the pollster examined. Ninety-four percent&nbsp;
of Republicans, 83 percent of independents,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:41.760
and 78 percent of Democrats were concerned.
The administration suggests that inflation&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:41.760 --> 00:00:46.320
increases are likely to be temporary, but the&nbsp;
polls suggest that Americans aren’t buying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:52.240
it – at least right now. In a late July CNBC&nbsp;
survey, 51 percent were pessimistic about the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:58.560
economy and the outlook, the highest level since&nbsp;
2015. Just 22 percent in the poll gave the economy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:04.640
positive marks and were optimistic. Joe Biden&nbsp;
is clearly losing ground on handling of the economy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:07.835
His honeymoon is clearly over.

00:01:07.835 --> 00:01:09.760
How worried are you about inflation?  

00:01:09.760 --> 00:01:14.160
Let us know in our poll. And also, let us know&nbsp;
what other topics you'd like our scholars to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:20.240
cover in 60 seconds, and be sure to like and&nbsp;
subscribe for more research and videos from AEI.

